                <pb facs="0445" n="393" xml:id="pg393"/>


                <head><hi rendition="#bold">Memorandum From the President’s Assistant for National
                        Security Affairs (Kissinger) to
                        Secretary of State Rogers</hi><anchor n="9" xml:id="d150-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1971-11-09">November 9, 1971</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Performing Arts Tour of the Soviet Union (S/S–7116533)</item>
                </list>
                <p>The President appreciated your report on Duke
                        Ellington’s recent, very successful tour of the Soviet Union.</p>
                <p>It is perhaps a bit early to take any decision concerning the desirability of
                    sending a performing arts group to the USSR to
                    coincide with the President’s planned visit. The President has indicated that he
                    will wish to weigh the pros and cons of such a proposal closer to the time of
                    the Moscow visit.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed corresp="#p_KHA_1">Henry A.
                            Kissinger</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
